From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Nov 2026 23:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1148 redfin: NFC persona: answer the NXP HDLL GET_VERSION in
 download mode with the EXACT bundled firmware version (not a high one)

STEP 3, following 1147's capture (PF/logs/research/nfc-ese-2026-11-16.md,
Follow-up 9). 1147 replied a HIGH version (ff ff); the k22 oslog shows nfcd
REJECTS it: phDnldNfc_DnldGetVersionCb's first gate is
`cmp bNewVer[1], bCurrVer[1]; b.hs` (requires bNewVer[1] >= bCurrVer[1]), so
bCurrVer[1]=0xff fails -> "MajorVerNum Mismatch" 0x3A, surfaced as status 0x00FF
(phLibNfc_SM_GetFwVersionTrans: Failed -> NFDriver _openDriver fails -> nfcd
hands off to nfrestore_service and loops in recovery ~every 2.7 s). The in-sync
branch needs EXACT equality bCurrVer[0]==bNewVer[0] && bCurrVer[1]==bNewVer[1].

bNewVer is read by nfcd/nfrestore from the bundled firmware image. The matching
bundle (hw id 0x42, major 2) is PN549_FW_02_01_5A_rev88207.bin. Read offline from
the iOS rootfs (HFS extract), its header is `00 e4 c0 00 5a 01 ...`; the two
version bytes live at offset 0x04 = `5a 01` = [FwMinor, FwMajor]. Confirmed by
the sibling bundles: PN548_FW_02_01_61 -> `61 01`, PN549_FW_03_01_60 -> `60 01`
(offset 0x04 byte always tracks the filename's last field, byte 0x05 is 01). So
bNewVer[0]=0x5a, bNewVer[1]=0x01, and the GET_VERSION reply payload P[3],P[4]
(=bCurrVer[0],bCurrVer[1]) must be `5a 01`.

This patch changes the download-mode GET_VERSION reply payload from
`42 02 01 ff ff 00 00 00` to `42 02 01 5a 01 00 00 00` and recomputes the HDLL
trailer with the shared nci_crc16 (CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE, poly 0x1021, init 0xFFFF,
big-endian, over the 10 LEN+payload bytes): 0x85ff -> 0xb1db. Emitted frame:
`00 08 42 02 01 5a 01 00 00 00 b1 db`. The send-time assertion now checks
c == 0xb1db. Every OTHER download-mode frame is still LOGGED ONLY (not answered)
so the next capture reveals whether nfcd, after a matching version, proceeds to
NCI resume or still forces a firmware WRITE.

SAFETY: unchanged from 1146/1147. Host-bound reply only; nothing reaches the
chip. Persona in gateway mode 0; gw_bus_ok()/sweet_nfc_tx_allowed() still block
all forwarding. No SPI/GPIO. Behind kern.sweet_nfc_fwif_fmt 0x40000 (with the
0x4000 eSE group), default-off. Test value stays 0x5D00 | 0x40000 = 0x45D00.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC2fg7dvyvbEkjpmxxg
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_nfc.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_nfc.c
index b99cc05..fddad9b 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_nfc.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_nfc.c
@@ -2680,29 +2680,32 @@ gw_packet_done(unsigned need, uint8_t *out, unsigned *no, unsigned cap, bool *wa
 	gw.pend = true;
 }
 
-/* 1147: reply to the NXP HDLL GET_VERSION read in download mode with a HIGH firmware version so nfcd treats the
- * chip firmware as in-sync and skips any firmware download/write. HDLL framing [LEN_hi LEN_lo | payload | CRC16],
+/* 1147/1148: reply to the NXP HDLL GET_VERSION read in download mode with the EXACT bundled firmware version so
+ * nfcd's major-version gate passes (ff ff is REJECTED: bNewVer[1] >= bCurrVer[1] fails -> 0x3A/0x00FF, recovery loop)
+ * and it treats the chip firmware as in-sync (no download/write). HDLL framing [LEN_hi LEN_lo | payload | CRC16],
  * CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE over LEN+payload (the same nci_crc16 the NCI persona uses). GET_VERSION response payload is 8
- * bytes: P[0]=0x42 (our hw id), P[3],P[4]=bCurrVer (ff ff = highest). Sent to the host over the same control unit
+ * bytes: P[0]=0x42 (our hw id), P[3],P[4]=bCurrVer. bCurrVer must EQUAL bNewVer read from the bundled image
+ * /usr/standalone/firmware/nfrestore/firmware/fw/PN549_FW_02_01_5A_rev88207.bin: header off 0x04 = 5a 01
+ * ([FwMinor,FwMajor]), so bCurrVer[0]=0x5a, bCurrVer[1]=0x01. Sent to the host over the same control unit
  * nfcd writes on; nothing reaches the chip. */
 static void
 gw_dl_reply_getversion(u_int32_t unit)
 {
-	uint8_t r[12] = { 0x00, 0x08, 0x42, 0x02, 0x01, 0xff, 0xff, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x85, 0xff };
-	uint16_t c = nci_crc16(r, 10);  /* over LEN+payload; must equal the 85 ff trailer */
+	uint8_t r[12] = { 0x00, 0x08, 0x42, 0x02, 0x01, 0x5a, 0x01, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0xb1, 0xdb };
+	uint16_t c = nci_crc16(r, 10);  /* over LEN+payload; must equal the b1 db trailer */
 
 	r[10] = (uint8_t)(c >> 8);
 	r[11] = (uint8_t)c;
-	if (c != 0x85ff) {
-		SAY("nfc-hci: persona: 1147: GET_VERSION CRC %04x != 85ff (not sent)\n", c);
+	if (c != 0xb1db) {
+		SAY("nfc-hci: persona: 1148: GET_VERSION CRC %04x != b1db (not sent)\n", c);
 		return;
 	}
 	if (gw_ctl != NULL && ctl_enqueuedata(gw_ctl, unit, r, sizeof(r), 0) == 0) {
 		gw_up_pkts++;
-		gw_hexlog("nfc-hci", r, sizeof(r), "dnld <persona GET_VERSION high reply, CRC16 85 ff");
+		gw_hexlog("nfc-hci", r, sizeof(r), "dnld <persona GET_VERSION exact-version reply 5a 01, CRC16 b1 db");
 	} else {
 		gw_up_fail++;
-		SAY("nfc-hci: persona: 1147: GET_VERSION reply send FAILED\n");
+		SAY("nfc-hci: persona: 1148: GET_VERSION reply send FAILED\n");
 	}
 }
 
